    "created_at": "2024-12-16T19:49:19Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-12-16T19:49:19Z",
    "body": "Nowadays, it is often possible to put an builtin element into an autonomous custom element with a `display: contents`. Not ideal, but it will work for some cases.\r\n\r\nHowever, in other cases, e.g. in tables, you are forced to use custom builtin elements.\r\nThen, if you want your custom tr to have a state, you are forced to use classes.\r\n\r\nThis is a pain as you might have some autonomous custom elements with ElementInternals states, and some custom builtin elements without but using classes. It'd be simpler to have an unique case to handle, instead of 2.\r\nNote: This is the same issue with shadowRoot, as some elements can have children, but can't have a shadowRoot, e.g. tr.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
